       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than double the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults. The 3,000 mg single dose is also about three times the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. At this level there is a serious risk of acute hepatotoxicity and liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day total), which is a common regimen.\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day), which is the standard maximum. Some clinicians use a lower cap of 3,000 mg/day.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, or another regimen.\n\nIf you really do want 3000 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
